Dataset content: {'instruction': 'Write a persuasive essay about why the voting age should be lowered.', 
'input': '', 'output': 'Lowering the voting age is an important step towards a better, more representative 
democracy. Young people, who make up a significant portion of the population, should have a say in their 
future and receive the same rights and benefits as adults. The young generation is very informed and 
conscious of the world’s current state, and is more likely to remain aware of their political environment 
as they age. Additionally, education plays a crucial role in the informed voting process, so it is 
important to note that the current voting age of 18 is set in many states just after high school 
graduation. Thus, young people are given the right to vote just when they become eligible to attend 
university, meaning they may not have received the necessary education.\n\nLowering the voting age also 
serves to engage younger people in civic participation, encouraging them to take an active role in 
politics, and ultimately leading to higher voter turnout for all age groups. Moreover, ultimately allowing 
youth to vote boosts civic engagement even beyond voting and encourages young people to express their 
thoughts and opinions.\n\nIn conclusion, the voting age should absolutely be lowered. Not only can it 
increase the number of politically-informed people, it can also simultaneously boost political enthusiasm 
overall. The youth should have the right and opportunity to participate in politics and be involved in 
one’s democracy and this could be realized by lowering the voting age.', 'text': 'Below is an instruction 
that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### 
Instruction:\nWrite a persuasive essay about why the voting age should be lowered.\n\n### 
Response:\nLowering the voting age is an important step towards a better, more representative democracy. 
Young people, who make up a significant portion of the population, should have a say in their future and 
receive the same rights and benefits as adults. The young generation is very informed and conscious of the 
world’s current state, and is more likely to remain aware of their political environment as they age. 
Additionally, education plays a crucial role in the informed voting process, so it is important to note 
that the current voting age of 18 is set in many states just after high school graduation. Thus, young 
people are given the right to vote just when they become eligible to attend university, meaning they may 
not have received the necessary education.\n\nLowering the voting age also serves to engage younger people 
in civic participation, encouraging them to take an active role in politics, and ultimately leading to 
higher voter turnout for all age groups. Moreover, ultimately allowing youth to vote boosts civic 
engagement even beyond voting and encourages young people to express their thoughts and opinions.\n\nIn 
conclusion, the voting age should absolutely be lowered. Not only can it increase the number of 
politically-informed people, it can also simultaneously boost political enthusiasm overall. The youth 
should have the right and opportunity to participate in politics and be involved in one’s democracy and 
this could be realized by lowering the voting age.', 'formatted_input': 'Write a persuasive essay about why
the voting age should be lowered.', 'turns': ['Write a persuasive essay about why the voting age should be 
lowered.']}

